@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Log Analytics & Alerts";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Log Analytics and Alerts in Azure DevOps provide powerful logging and monitoring capabilities, helping teams diagnose issues, track system health, and proactively respond to incidents.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Log Analytics?</h2>
        <p>Azure Log Analytics is a cloud-based service that collects and analyzes log data from various sources, including Azure resources, virtual machines, and applications.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Centralized Logging:</strong> Collect logs from multiple services and applications in a single workspace.</li>
            <li><strong>Real-Time Insights:</strong> Use Kusto Query Language (KQL) to analyze log data.</li>
            <li><strong>Security & Compliance:</strong> Track access logs and detect potential security threats.</li>
            <li><strong>Performance Monitoring:</strong> Identify slow response times and application failures.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/monitoring/media/log-analytics-overview.png" alt="Azure Log Analytics Dashboard" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Log Analytics in Action</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What are Azure Alerts?</h2>
        <p>Azure Alerts notify DevOps teams when specific conditions occur in monitored resources, enabling proactive issue resolution.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Threshold-Based Alerts:</strong> Trigger notifications when resource usage exceeds predefined limits.</li>
            <li><strong>Log-Based Alerts:</strong> Set alerts based on specific log events.</li>
            <li><strong>Integration with Incident Management:</strong> Connect alerts to Azure DevOps, Slack, Microsoft Teams, or PagerDuty.</li>
            <li><strong>Automated Remediation:</strong> Configure auto-scaling and self-healing mechanisms.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/monitoring/media/alerts-dashboard.png" alt="Azure Alerts Dashboard" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Configuring Alerts in Azure Monitor</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Setting Up Log Analytics & Alerts</h3>
        <p>Follow these steps to configure Log Analytics and Alerts:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Create a Log Analytics Workspace:</strong> Go to Azure Portal > Monitor > Log Analytics Workspaces > Create.</li>
            <li><strong>Connect Data Sources:</strong> Add virtual machines, containers, or Azure services.</li>
            <li><strong>Query Logs Using KQL:</strong> Use the Azure Log Analytics query editor for data analysis.</li>
            <li><strong>Define an Alert Rule:</strong> Navigate to Azure Monitor > Alerts > Create a new alert rule.</li>
            <li><strong>Set Action Groups:</strong> Configure email, SMS, or webhook notifications.</li>
            <li><strong>Automate Incident Response:</strong> Integrate alerts with auto-remediation scripts.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Example YAML for Alert Configuration</h3>
        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
steps:
- task: AzureMonitorAlerts@1
  inputs:
    azureSubscription: 'MyAzureSubscription'
    resourceGroupName: 'MyResourceGroup'
    alertRuleName: 'HighMemoryUsage'
    conditionOperator: 'GreaterThan'
    conditionThreshold: '75'
    actionGroup: 'DevOpsTeamAlerts'
        </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Best Practices for Log Analytics & Alerts</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Enable Log Retention Policies:</strong> Store logs for a sufficient period to support compliance.</li>
            <li><strong>Use Actionable Alerts:</strong> Reduce noise by setting meaningful alert thresholds.</li>
            <li><strong>Integrate with DevOps Tools:</strong> Send alerts to incident management tools like Jira, ServiceNow, or Azure DevOps.</li>
            <li><strong>Automate Responses:</strong> Configure auto-healing and auto-scaling based on alert conditions.</li>
            <li><strong>Regularly Review & Optimize:</strong> Adjust alert settings to prevent false positives.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>By leveraging Azure Log Analytics and Alerts, DevOps teams can gain deep visibility into system health, proactively address issues, and ensure continuous application availability.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-start mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("AzureMonitorInsights", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Azure Monitor & Application Insights</a>
    </div>
</div>